1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,960
So this particular day I had a really busy uh schedule which I had blocked out starting at 6 30 in the morning.
那一天我的日程非常忙，我已经分好了时间，从早上六点半开始安排。

2
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:10,519
I didn't want to get up too early cuz I knew it was going to be a long day.
我不想起得太早，因为我知道这会是漫长的一天。

3
00:00:10,519 --> 00:00:16,790
So I wanted to get my coffee going and then I also wanted to make the kids lunches typically my husband is on lunch patrol.
所以我想先煮上咖啡，再给孩子们做午餐。通常准备午餐是我丈夫负责。

4
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:24,480
But this particular day he had to go check on a vineyard project really early and then he was going to come back and help me with a drop off.
但那天他很早就得去查看一个葡萄园项目，之后再回来帮我送孩子。

5
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,160
I missed the days when my kids are really young and loved bento boxes.
我怀念孩子们还小、喜欢便当盒的时候。

6
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:38,680
But they seem to be eating so much more now that they're getting older that I feel bad only giving them a bento box cuz there's not as much food as I can probably give them in the bag.
但他们长大以后似乎吃得多多了，只给一个便当盒我会觉得不太够，因为袋子里大概能装更多食物。

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:43,559
So today I just thought it'd be easy to make some sandwiches some healthy fruit options for them.
所以今天我觉得做一些三明治，再给他们配些我认为健康的水果，比较省事。

8
00:00:43,559 --> 00:00:50,520
Tell us in the comments down below if you are a mom or a caregiver of children what is your routine and how many kids do you have.
如果你是妈妈，或者负责照顾孩子，欢迎在下面评论，你的日常怎么安排，有几个孩子？

9
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:56,800
If you're new here I have four children um all in the elementary school level well one is actually in junior high.
如果你刚来，我有四个孩子，都在小学阶段，嗯，其实有一个已经上初中了。

10
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:00,040
But it's all at the same school so it always feels like it's the same.
不过他们都在同一所学校，所以总觉得差不多。

11
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:06,030
But my morning routine typically does not involved making lunches um sometimes I'll make breakfast just kind of depends.
但我平时早上的日常通常不包括做午餐。有时候我会做早餐，要看情况。

12
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:14,319
But I try to use these hours I call them fringe hours so before 7 when the kids get up and after 9 30 after the kids are all asleep.
我尽量利用这些时间，我叫它们“边角时间”：孩子们七点起床前，还有晚上九点半以后，他们都睡着的时候。

13
00:01:14,319 --> 00:01:25,320
I try to do as much work in those hours as I can especially since I have multiple different jobs um that's how I'm able to compartmentalize u multiple responsibilities throughout the day so um.
我尽可能在这些时段多做工作，尤其是我有好几份不同的工作。这样才能在一天中把多种职责分开处理。

14
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:33,720
And then I have my obviously my main job which is um somewhat 9 to 5 not really I mean I get to work around 8 15 every day um.
然后还有我的主要工作，算是朝九晚五，也不完全是，我每天大概八点十五到单位。

15
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:36,520
But then I work at home and I'm kind of all over the place.
不过我也在家工作，工作地点和安排比较分散。

16
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:44,880
I also typically work 6 days a week so for me it's really nice to be able to have um these like fringe hours to be able to work.
我通常每周工作六天，所以能有这些边角时间处理工作，对我来说挺好。

17
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:51,920
So that's where my husband will do lunches um usually between 6 00 and 700 um and get all the lunches and uh breakfast ready.
所以丈夫通常会在六点到七点之间做午餐，把午餐和早餐都准备好。

18
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:59,280
While I do a little bit of pre prep for the day get all my emails out and really try to set the day off on um kind of a good note.
与此同时，我会先做一点当天的准备，发掉所有邮件，尽量让一天有个好的开头。

19
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:05,800
The other thing I like about sending emails first thing in the morning is by the time I get to the office um most of those folks have already responded to me.
我喜欢一大早发邮件的另一个原因是，等我到办公室，大多数人已经回复我了。

20
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:13,040
But this particular day I needed to get lunch is done so we are going to do that tell us in the comments down below what are your routines.
不过那天我得把午餐做好，那就先做这个。也在下面评论说说你们的日常安排。

21
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,880
We always try to keep the kids lunches as balanced as possible.
我们总会尽量让孩子们的午餐搭配均衡。

22
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:58,280
So always having a vegetable always having a fruit and then a good protein um I like to add like yogurt or a string cheese.
所以总会有蔬菜、水果，再加一份蛋白质食物。我喜欢加酸奶或者一根奶酪条。

23
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,599
Or something like that is always really good for the kids.
或者诸如此类的东西，我觉得给孩子们吃挺好。

24
00:03:00,599 --> 00:03:09,000
We've also been um letting them pick out their sid so if they want goldfish or chips or something like that they can go in the pantry and pick those things out.
最近我们也让他们自己选配菜或小零食，如果想吃 Goldfish 饼干或者薯片，他们就能进食品储藏柜挑。

25
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:14,640
Sometime in the near future I think maybe next year we're going to let the kids start packing their own lunches.
在不远的将来，我想也许明年，我们会开始让孩子们自己打包午餐。

26
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:23,959
Um again they're ranging in different ages but um right now it's just too hectic with the little ones to then um have some of them making their lunches and some not.
他们年龄也各不相同，但现在有小孩子在，一切太忙乱了，再让其中一些人自己做午餐、另一些不做，就更难安排。
